      "narrative": "Little Giant, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. Transfer of command from CIMT (NW Team 13) to CIMT (NW Team 12) will occur today. CIMT is also managing the Sisi incident. Thirty miles northwest of Leavenworth, WA. Timber and dormant brush. Minimal fire behavior with creeping, backing and smoldering. Structures threatened. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Sisi, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. Ten miles northwest of Stehekin, WA. Closed timber litter and timber. Moderate fire behavior with backing, flanking and creeping. Residences threatened. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Austin, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. CIMT (CA Team 2). CIMT is also managing The Narrows and Grasshopper incidents. Twenty-five miles southeast of Estacada, OR. Brush, timber and closed timber litter. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering and creeping. Area, road and trail closures in effect. The Narrows, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. Fifteen miles southeast of Estacada, OR. Grass, brush and light slash. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Grasshopper, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. Fourteen miles southwest of Dufur, OR. Brush, hardwood litter and closed timber litter. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering and creeping. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Hagen, Umatilla NF, USFS. Twenty-six miles east of Pendleton, OR. Timber. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Sinlahekin, Northeast Region, Washington DNR. One mile west of Tonasket, WA. Timber, brush and grass. Minimal fire behavior with creeping and smoldering. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Three Queens, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. Six miles east of Snoqualmie Pass, WA. Timber, brush and grass. No new information."
